# The front end reports that it could not prove the negative-literal i8 ensure, and so the run's
# verification state stays open; the proof engine proves and replays every obligation regardless.
# The report says so, instead of leaving an open state with no failed goal to explain it (BACKLOG K-07).
def keep(x: i8) -> i8:
    ensure result == x
    ensure result >= -128
    return x
